23:15:13.784 advertise: AUTO - each client is told the host it can actually reach:
23:15:13.784   a client on a private, loopback, link-local or CGNAT address is told the
23:15:13.784   address it reached this server on; a client on a public address is told
23:15:13.784   this box's public address, below.
23:15:13.784   public address: 203.0.113.42 (from checkip.amazonaws.com, re-checked every 10 min)
23:15:13.784   channel 0: port 8485, host decided per connection
23:15:13.784   channel 1: port 8486, host decided per connection
23:15:13.784 NOT AUTHENTICATED: a migration seed is a u32, so it identifies a pending
23:15:13.784   migration rather than proving who is on the far end. It is single-use.
23:15:13.784 THIS CHANNEL ANSWERS PACKETS - the default since 2026-09-14. It used to need
23:15:13.784   --set-field-probe, a flag every caller passed and whose absence cost a launch;
23:15:13.784   --silent-channel is the way to turn answering off now, and it is only for
23:15:13.784   eliminating the channel as a variable.
23:15:13.784   This channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
23:15:13.784   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
23:15:13.784   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
23:15:13.784   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
23:15:13.784   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
23:15:13.785   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
23:15:13.785   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
23:15:13.785   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
23:15:13.785   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
